claimed: backlog-dedup — channel-impls listed UnboundedCasChannel (Michael-Scott) as a separate implementation alongside channel-ring-unbounded (segmented ring). They are not independent: a segmented ring dominates MS on every axis (amortises allocation over a segment instead of a node per element, cache-friendly, no per-element node), and it is the Segmented Queue construction Koch-Sanders-Williams 2025 SS3 surveys. Merge the two entries into one, keeping the distinction from StmChannel stated precisely (3 allocations per push and a whole-state CAS, against 1 node and a single-pointer CAS) so the next lane does not re-derive it.
